    "dc.description.abstract": [
      {
        "value": "NOMAD provides an integrated electronic laboratory notebook (ELN) for documenting and managing materials science experiments. Researchers can create structured, searchable records of substances, samples, instruments, processing steps, measurements, and analyses, and link them to represent complete experimental workflows. Built-in ELN templates can be used directly in the web interface, while custom templates can be defined using YAML schemas. Institutions and research groups can deploy NOMAD Oasis on their own infrastructure and extend its ELN functionality through Python-based schema plugins.\n\nNOMAD Central Platform is a free web service for organizing, analyzing, sharing, and publishing materials science data. Its integrated ELN connects laboratory documentation with experimental and computational data, supporting collaboration and reuse. All data in NOMAD are organized in well-defined structures described by a formal schema to support the FAIR principles (Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, Reusable). Researchers can explore, download, and analyze publicly available data and assign a Digital Object Identifier (DOI) to a published project so others can cite it.",
        "language": null,
        "authority": null,
        "confidence": -1,
        "place": 0
      }
    ],
